@lang en
IMPORT `baominh-par-conditions`

-- Bao Minh property all risks rules: THE CLAIM, all three layers joined.
-- Nothing here is new law: each step calls the module for the clause that says it.
--
--   1. The general conditions: forfeiture (GC 4(a), 10), the premium warranty (GC 15), and the
--      conditions precedent (GC 5, 9, 11, 12, 13). Any failure: nothing is payable.
--   2. Item by item: the insuring clause (Damage, premises, period, premium), GC 2
--      (misdescription), GC 8 (alteration), then the exclusions.
--   3. The amount: each item's measure, exclusion 9, GC 14, GC 6, the item's sum insured; then
--      the loss's caps and the deductible.

§ `The claim`

§§ `One item`

-- Why the item, on its own facts, yields nothing: the insuring clause, GC 2, GC 8, or an
-- exclusion that takes the Damage out wholly. Empty where something may be payable on it.
@ref insuring clause (src:7-19); General Conditions 2 and 8; exclusions (src:27-248)
GIVEN s IS A `The Schedule`
      l IS A `A loss`
      i IS A `A damaged item`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`why nothing is payable on the item` s l i MEANS
    IF   NOT null `before the exclusions`
    THEN `before the exclusions`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the effect of the exclusions on` l i
         WHEN `excluded by` cl THEN cl
         WHEN `no exclusion applies` THEN EMPTY
         WHEN `excluded except for the part arising from a cause not excluded` cl THEN EMPTY
    WHERE
        `before the exclusions` MEANS
            concat (LIST (`why the insuring clause does not reach the item` s l i)
                       , (`why General Condition 2 takes the item out` i)
                       , (`why General Condition 8 takes the item out` i))

@ref insuring clause (src:16-26); exclusions; General Conditions 6, 14
GIVEN s IS A `The Schedule`
      l IS A `A loss`
      i IS A `A damaged item`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount for the item in the claim` s l i MEANS
    IF   null (`why nothing is payable on the item` s l i)
    THEN `the amount for the item` i `given` (`the effect of the exclusions on` l i)
    ELSE 0

§§ `The answer`

@export What Bao Minh must pay under its Property All Risks rules for one loss, or why nothing is payable, with every reason traceable to a clause
GIVEN s IS A `The Schedule` @desc The Schedule (Bản tóm lược hợp đồng bảo hiểm): the period, the items and their sums insured, the limits, the deductible and the premium
      l IS A `A loss`       @desc One loss: its date, whether it is sudden physical Damage, each item damaged with its chain of causation and valuation, and the Insured's conduct
GIVETH A `The answer for a claim`
`the answer for the claim` s l MEANS
    IF   NOT null (`why the general conditions defeat the claim` s l)
    THEN `nothing is payable because` (`why the general conditions defeat the claim` s l)
    ELSE IF   `the amount` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `the Insurer must pay` `the amount`
         ELSE `nothing is payable because`
                  (append (concat (map (GIVEN i YIELD `why nothing is payable on the item` s l i) (l's `the damaged items`)))
                          (LIST "the amount for the loss, after the conditions, the caps and the deductible, is nil"))
    WHERE
        `the amount` MEANS
            `the amount for the loss` s (map (GIVEN i YIELD `the amount for the item in the claim` s l i) (l's `the damaged items`))
